{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514338-original-clan","id":1514338,"title":"Original Clan","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-09T14:33:45-07:00","id":1514338,"title":"Original Clan","content":"Basically I read the conversation about Caitiff and theories that they can establish a new clan, but anyway what I remembered in this story is that there was a time when the bushin clan was created, at least that's the name I remember, which was a different clan that even had its own weakness, you can't swear falsely, anyway, I wanted to know if anyone here has already tried to create an original clan and run an experiment with it, I've tried it twice myself, but this is more complicated than that I expected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T21:04:53-07:00","id":1514391,"title":"","content":"I sometimes play with creating Bloodlines. One of this, for example, are the Jezebel Childrens, or Abrahelites. They are the childrens of a relative old Ministry that obtenied Vicissitude, and his fledlings and the fledlings have Vicissitud instead of Serpentis. They have the typical Setite/Ministry curse, and cant stay more than one month having the same gender","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28021-camaradadoppio","name":"CamaradaDoppio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28021_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T01:58:22-07:00","id":1514429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514338-original-clan#post1514338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> bushin clan</div> </div> </div> </div>Before the release of Kindred of the East, the Gaki were considered an exotic bloodline of Cainites who used the Discipline of Rift. These older depictions were retconned to instead reflect the incomplete picture Western Kindred have of their Asian brethren, similarly, the Bushi were considered an exotic bloodline of Cainites who used the Discipline of Rift.<br /> They not really had any ties to the Caitiff to be honest - or at least as I can remember; Dark Alliance: Vancouver not went in to deep details about them<br /> After Kindred of the East came out, the Bushi became House Bishamon one of the two major uji of the Clans of the Sun (Clans of the Sun are the umbrella group of the collective Kuei-jin of Japan, who call themselves Gaki.), the other is House Genji<br /> House Bishamon became a traditionalist society concearned with Dharmic redemption, while Hosue Genji established a wild and loose uji heavily involved in Japan's modern corporate culture (while the Hosues of Iga, Koga, Nukekubi, Echizen, Taira, Hiyorumi and Sotogawa No a minor uji)<br /> The Gaki (or Ketsuki), became the collective name of the Japanese Kuei-jin and fall into extended \u201cClans\u201d or \u201cHouses\u201d called uji. Each uji may claim several cities as their territory, though small uji are restricted to a single urban area. This structure imitates the mortal aristocratic clans, like the Fujiwara or Minamoto, who dominate Japan for much of its history. Of course these vampiric \u201cfamilies\u201d grow only through adoption.<br /> Mor about this in Kindred of the East Rulebook\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514338-original-clan#post1514338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically I read the conversation about Caitiff and theories that they can establish a new clan (...) wanted to know if anyone here has already tried to create an original clan and run an experiment with it, I've tried it twice myself, but this is more complicated than that I expected.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Bloodline is a term used to describe a group of vampires who share a common lineage. While the term can be used to refer to vampires who share a sire, grandsire, or so on, it usually refers to those lineages that have some inherent distinction from the thirteen traditional clans of Caine, be it in their weaknesses, Disciplines, or both. Many of these bloodlines are, in effect, a clan within a clan.<br /> The childe of a vampire who belongs to a bloodline will always belong to the same bloodline as her sire, and there is no traditional method to change one's lineage. Therefore, bloodlines are generally the product of unique supernatural events, and are functionally just smaller clans. Bloodlines are not necessarily tied to specific clans, however, and they are created in a variety of ways:<br /> <b>Mystical methods </b>- Some bloodlines are created through mystic rituals that transform their founders, such as with the Gargoyles and Kiasyd, albeit not necessarily deliberately.<br /> <b>Flawed Embrace </b>- Sometimes, for whatever reason, a childe does not inherit their sire's clan, instead becoming something different, as seen with the Maeghar, the Caitiff, and even potentially with the Baali founders.<br /> <b>Divergent evolution</b> - A bloodline splits off from the clan when they are geographically isolated from the parent clan and develop their own customs, such as with the Anda.<br /> <b>Convergent evolution</b> - The reverse of the former method, and a subset of the first. Through extrinsic mystical changes in the blood, Kindred of an existing bloodline who choose to associate with another (or more specific) clan may eventually begin to exhibit characteristics in common with mainline members of the clan, losing their old curses and compulsions in favor of those of their new compatriots. This has evidently been the case for the Nagaraja and Samedi who have chosen to join Clan Hecata.<br /> <b>Independent origin</b> - Some bloodlines claim no connection with the clans, having arisen independently through encounters with gods, spirits, and eldritch entities, such as the Bonsam, Impundulu, and Ramanga.<br /> <b>Diablerie of Antediluvian</b> - All clans have their own Antediluvians; on more than one occasion, that Antediluvian has been replaced, resulting in the original clan being &quot;demoted&quot; to bloodline status. The Harbingers of Skulls, Salubri, and True Brujah bloodlines can all claim this distinction.<br /> Additionally, some variants of the Blood do not <i>necessarily</i> qualify for full bloodline status, and might be described as mere variations of the clans<br /> For the most part, these are offshoots of the main clans that differ only in outlook or culture, but are generally considered by Cainite society to still belong to their parent clan \u2013 Salubri antitribu are still Salubri, and the Assamite Vizier caste are still Assamites. In other cases, some of these minor bloodlines can display different weaknesses or clan disciplines, showing signs of divergent evolution. These subtle differences might not be visible to outside observers, but they are part of what makes vampiric society so diverse and confusing. Here are some causes for the minor variations of the Blood:<br /> <b>Caste system </b>- some clans are separated into caste systems, with certain castes possessing different disciplines and weaknesses from the parent clan. Certain clans (the Assamites, Ravnos, Salubri, Setites, and Tzimisce in particular) have internal variants with different attributes and Embraces, but which are still socially part of the parent clan.<br /> <b>Differing beliefs</b> - In some cases, Clan Variants arise in the case of cultural and /or geographical splits from the main Clan without diverging into a full fledged bloodline. Examples are the Old Clan Tzimisce, the Telyavelic Tremere and the Daitya.<br /> <b>Antitribu</b> - also known as anti-clan, are groups that have diverged from their parent clan in order to join a different sect. Largely a social division, the antitribu frequently begin to demonstrate slightly different weaknesses, and then different disciplines altogether. This is largely an early example of divergent evolution.<br /> Finally, there is the case of the Laibon. These African vampires may be examples of divergent evolution, or they may actually be members of the standard clans, but simply known under a different name. As with many variations of the blood, the truth can be uncertain<br /> <br /> There are pelnty of ways to create a Bloodline as you can see, and I created several for my games, or let my players to be a member of their own bloodline, as long as the Backstory was sufficiently detailed<br /> <br /> Creating a Clan is similar<br /> Just create a Progenitor<br /> As long as the Players okay with it tho'&lt; it is nice and all to be all powerfull Storyteller and create what you want, but never hurt to have the approval of the Palyers - I have quite a few who were more orthodox when it came to stories and I could understand them\u200b<br /> But many others were thrilled by the idea of the unknown, alternate Cainitevampire orogins and so on<br /> I have somewhere a topic about this somwhere on the forum <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T03:11:25-07:00","id":1514437,"title":"","content":"Their was a caitiff/pander in the a mates who diablerised his way up to 8th gen game at which state the blood 'calcified' into a bloodline. Disciplines were obfuscate, animalism and Fortitude clan flaw was a bought one....curious I think. Bloodlines gimmick was deliberately avoiding high density areas and living in rural towns. Nominally Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-10-2023, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T06:34:43-07:00","id":1514461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514338-original-clan?p=1514437#post1514437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their was a caitiff/pander in the a mates who diablerised his way up to 8th gen game at which state the blood 'calcified' into a bloodline. Disciplines were obfuscate, animalism and Fortitude clan flaw was a bought one....curious I think. Bloodlines gimmick was deliberately avoiding high density areas and living in rural towns. Nominally Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's this weakness thing that gets me to tell you the truth, I tried to create a clan and I went crazy trying to think of a weakness that made sense. The closest I came to a conclusion was a weakness that causes numbness (similar to alcoholism) or kindred needing enzymes to &quot;cook&quot; the blood before consumption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T07:03:53-07:00","id":1514466,"title":"","content":"I play with a house rule that Caitiff and Thin Blood effectively mean the same thing, and if a Thin Blood eats a full blooded vampire, he becomes the founder of his own Bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T06:40:49-07:00","id":1515653,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Caitiff being a social function and less a biological. A degoratory catch-all term that describes a kindred rejected by society or perhaps never even accepted by it in the first place. <br /> <br /> They all have a clan by blood, some of them does not know their heritage but that is by no means a must. What is common for all Caitiff in my WoD is that they are barred from the social structure the clans represent. The equillent of being driven out of town in past times. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27829-mallgoth","name":"Mallgoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T09:28:54-07:00","id":1515673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mallgoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514338-original-clan?p=1515653#post1515653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of Caitiff being a social function and less a biological. A degoratory catch-all term that describes a kindred rejected by society or perhaps never even accepted by it in the first place.<br /> <br /> They all have a clan by blood, some of them does not know their heritage but that is by no means a must. What is common for all Caitiff in my WoD is that they are barred from the social structure the clans represent. The equillent of being driven out of town in past times.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It seems that you and I think of this topic in very much the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T22:23:56-07:00","id":1515720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514338-original-clan#post1514338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically I read the conversation about Caitiff and theories that they can establish a new clan, but anyway what I remembered in this story is that there was a time when the bushin clan was created, at least that's the name I remember, which was a different clan that even had its own weakness, you can't swear falsely, anyway, I wanted to know if anyone here has already tried to create an original clan and run an experiment with it, I've tried it twice myself, but this is more complicated than that I expected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could be completely wrong on that, but for me it sounds like you're describing a mix of several ramblings of Dr. Solomon Grey, the &quot;scholar on clanless&quot; and in-character narrator of the Caitff chapter of the (very outdated) <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Outcasts:_A_Players_Guide_to_Pariahs\" target=\"_blank\">Outcasts</a> sourcebook. I'm pretty sure it is THE one book to explore the idea of Caitiff as creators of new disciplines and bloodlines (even though it ran completely counter to the presentation of canon bloodlines before or since) and i suspect, perhaps a major inspiration for many concepts later retooled into Thin Bloods as we know them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514338-original-clan?p=1514429#post1514429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Before the release of Kindred of the East, the Gaki were considered an exotic bloodline of Cainites who used the Discipline of Rift. These older depictions were retconned to instead reflect the incomplete picture Western Kindred have of their Asian brethren, similarly, the Bushi were considered an exotic bloodline of Cainites who used the Discipline of Rift.<br /> They not really had any ties to the Caitiff to be honest - or at least as I can remember; Dark Alliance: Vancouver not went in to deep details about them</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Close, but not quite - while there's some hefty amount of weeb pretensions at &quot;vampire modern samurai&quot; mixed in, the Bushi, (or Children of Susanoo, as they are also called in Dark Alliance: Vancouver and i have much prefered to use as formal name for them through the years), were presented much closer to the usual format for clans &amp; bloodlines, with Celerity, Presence &amp; Kai for disciplines.<br /> <br /> When it comes to weaknesses, there was much talking over the subject of truth, lying, honor and the colaterals - social and spiritual/mechanical - of breaking one's given word. But it was also kind of confusing in that it also repeatedly referenced the Gaki or WtA's own honor system, kind of implying that it wasn't properly a weakness of the Bushi so much as a honor sub-system supposed to apply to japanese vampires like the Gaki, Children of Susanoo (or others of one's own creation) equally.<br /> <br /> That said, the Children of Susanoo did also have <i>as a weakness of their own</i> a greater susceptibility to sunlight, supposedly due to a curse of Amaterasu on their progenitor (it also makes for a interesting potential connection to Setites if one considers the figure of Orochi).<br /> <br /> Kai had no connection to <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Rift\" target=\"_blank\">Rift</a> whatsoever and as a discipline was kind of a mish-mash of &quot;oriental movie&quot; tropes i'd say, but one can see for their own <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Kai\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. (And the KotE's writers trying to handwave it as <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Kiai\" target=\"_blank\">Kiai</a> was kind of ridiculous)\u200b<br /> <br /> Since my version of Southeast Asia is something of a mix of 1st ed WoD, DAl:V and a bastaridzed version of KotE in kindred form, Children of Susanoo are still very much around in my games - specially in the form of recurring NPC archon Mariko, aka &quot;gothic lolita Mary Poppins of the lightning umbrella&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Kai i very much replaced with some wind, storm &amp; lightning-themed powers about the time i decided to keep the Children around and ignore Year of the Lotus canon)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mallgoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514338-original-clan?p=1515653#post1515653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of Caitiff being a social function and less a biological. A degoratory catch-all term that describes a kindred rejected by society or perhaps never even accepted by it in the first place.<br /> <br /> They all have a clan by blood, some of them does not know their heritage but that is by no means a must. What is common for all Caitiff in my WoD is that they are barred from the social structure the clans represent. The equillent of being driven out of town in past times.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the jargon of the ageless undead is as vulnerable to the vagaries of fashion, prejudice and memetic mutation as that of mortals, so words change meaning, get distorted with times and so on.<br /> <br /> In my games the terms Caitiff &amp; thin-blood tend to be used interchangeably by &quot;polite&quot; kindred society.<br /> <br /> Between anarchs it can vary depending on how much of a community of their own a domain's local anarchs are - some might ape the courts with little to no self-awareness of the disparaging essence of the terms, while anarch groups more conscious and sensitive to the built-in prejudices might gravitate toward terms such as &quot;clanless&quot;, &quot;unbound&quot; or even &quot;duskborn&quot;, depending on one's specific origin or condition.<br /> <br /> For centuries the Sabbat would sit somewhere between those two extremes, with great variety depending on one's faction, lineage or coven/pack dynamics, but everything would change with the rise of the Panders as a faction - ever since, Joseph's followers have made considerable effort to convert many kindred, clanless or not, to their movement/clan and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Joseph_Pander\" target=\"_blank\">initiation</a> into &quot;truly breaking the chains of the Founders&quot;.<br /> <br /> (For what i must thank the writers of <b>Rites of the Blood</b>, specially whoever came up with the <i>One of My Tribe</i>\u200b and its roots on Native American initiation and manhood rites. Even with little to no mechanics, just the concept of it changed everything for me about the portrayal of the Panders in relation to Caitiff and Thin-Blood, not to mention turning Joseph Pander in a major antagonist of my Milwaukee/BJD chronicle right beside Vykos, Carna &amp; Parovich).\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-08-2026, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}